he time  she was under no obligation to  thoroughly research the claims that she  made about voter fraud in the lawsuit  she sort of made the case at the time  listen people came to me and they said  this is what happened  and it's not up to me to independently  verify that that's what the case is i'm  just the lawyer here which the judge  does not agree with and it makes  absolutely no sense  um  in this week's filing powell and  kleinhandler casually admit  everything they had been saying may not  actually be true  but because lots of people were saying  it at the time they decided to include  it quote millions of americans believe  the central contentions of the complaint  to be true  and perhaps they are  admitting she's no longer actually  confident  about the veracity of those claims now  i think it's important to ask the  question  does she believe all of these wacky  election claims are true but she's  backing off because of the legal  problems that she's now happening she's  now having  did she never believe the claims were  true or did she believe them and she has  since changed her mind  legally speaking i don't know that it  makes a difference  um as a reminder  here are some of the wacky things that  this woman said  the amount of evidence that this  election was completely fraudulent and  that joe biden is a fraudulent president  is beyond overwhelming now understand  that  if we are to believe her current  statement  what she meant when she said that was  the people i'm working with told me this  but i don't really know it to be true  that's what she now says listen we were  told these things we didn't  independently confirm them here's  another sydney powell clip so  i don't know where to go next because  this is like something out of a movie so  the department of defense let's review  yeah 2006 a patent coming from the  department of defense that allows for  algorithm that can flip and change votes  the patent was transferred to i love the  reference to an algorithm  it's an algorithm  it can predetermine that algorithm can  predetermine the outcome of an election  it's specifically to  uh  create a predetermined outcome okay so  maybe she believed that to be true at  the time or again maybe that's just what  some of the people she was working with  told her um here's another one about a  secret server what i think really has to  be  discovered is that there is a secret  server that all the votes go to where  they manipulate the heck out of it now  did she believe that at the time or was  that also just something people were  telling her and here's one last one with  this wacky guy stu peters  that for at least 20 years now  somebody other than the voters of the  united states of america has been  determining  certain elections and this year if not  prior years it happened to be the  presidency of the united states of  america now did she believe that at the  time  or again was it just we were told that  stuff and we didn't investigate it so  sydney powell now saying ah we don't  really know that any of that stuff was  true it's just what we were told just  what we were told by plaintiffs uh she's  really uh potentially in trouble here  and i think that's all that's going on  let me know your thoughts find me on  twitter at d pacman  if you or someone you know is into  science astronomy space this is for you  our sponsor under lucky stars creates  beautiful personalized star maps  showing the unique position of the stars  in the sky  at the place and time chosen by you  under lucky stars is a great way to  remember an important moment someone's  birthday wedding day your engagement you  give them a time and a location that you  want to commemorate they show you  exactly how the stars and constellations  looked in a spectacular super high  quality print to completely personalized  gift experience you can customize it  into a ton of designs you can read on  their website how all the star maps are  scientifically